javisfelagund@yahoo.com.mx (Javis Felagund) writes:
> Just a question... in earlier versions of NH it used to say that Sting
> glows blue whenever you know who were near. Now the effect is kind of
> changed, and you can actually see them. I know that's better, I'm not
> complaining.

> Was it because the 'glow blue' message is confussing with the one a
> ?oEW gives?

Not as far as I know. The old warning system used to give intermittent
messages, glowing rings or sensed flashes, and had a timing mechanism
to track how often to give them (warnlevel, lastwarnlev, lastwarntime,
and warnDelay); Sting's warning of orcs hooked into that. When the
new, constant, warning system replaced it, that timing system was
removed; I imagine it was considered impractical to retain it just for
Sting.

(Actually, all the old code is still there, just defined out. So that
really ought to be worded "impractical to extract only the parts
needed to maintain Sting's behaviour".)

